<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tocco family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tocco were an Italian noble family of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kefalonia">Cephalonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakynthos">Zakynthos</a> and Leucas from 1357 and, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlo-i-tocco">Carlo I Tocco</a>, also <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannina">Ioannina</a> and Arta. Ottoman conquest stripped them of the mainland in the mid-15th century and of the islands in 1479, after which the family returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tocco-family.jpg" alt="Tocco family" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Constantine Plakidas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_Tocco_family.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Squeezed between the Despotate of the Morea, Venice, the <b>Tocco</b> rulers of Epirus and Ottoman raiders, he lost ground steadily.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1357 the county passed to Leonardo I Tocco, and his son Carlo I Tocco extended <b>Tocco</b> power to Ioannina and Arta.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-palatine-of-cephalonia-and-zakynthos">County Palatine of Cephalonia and Zakynthos</a></li><li><blockquote>They fought the Angevins, the <b>Tocco of Kefalonia</b>, the Navarrese Company and the Ottomans.</blockquote><a href="/state/despotate-of-angelokastron-and-lepanto">Despotate of Angelokastron and Lepanto</a></li></ul></section>
